    "poweredBy": "Powered by Viator",
    "description": "On this two-hour tour, you’ll get the opportunity to take a bike ride around Lower Manhattan and climb uphill to enjoy the panoramic views of New York Harbour.\r\n\r\nAlong the way, your guide will tell you stories about the past of New York and will share facts about the origins of the city’s famous attractions. You’ll be able to discover New York City Hall, Ellis Island and the Statue of Liberty, Staten Island and the Financial District.\r\n\r\nAfter a 15-minute climb, you’ll then reach the Brooklyn Bridge and cross it to see the city from the opposite side. Before the tour ends, you’ll also have the chance to explore the South Street Seaport area.",
